    "explanation": "To both parties: the rider's dispute is partly upheld. The recorded route distances show the driver travelled 11.5 km against a recommended 9.9 km — a deviation of 1.60 km — which is over the 1.0 km tolerance in POL-RD-22, so this is not a within-tolerance case. The driver did not inform the rider of the reroute: the trip's chat log carries 0 messages and there are no in-app calls or call recordings in the record, so under POL-RD-21 the deviation was not notified and not agreed. On traffic justification, POL-RD-23 admits only congestion, an incident or a closure shown by traffic data that intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window. The advisory covering the very KPE segment the driver left (EV-ADVIS-06006-01, Hougang Avenue 2 exit to PIE) is type NONE — no incident, roadwork or closure, speed bands 5-6 throughout. The only advisory of an admissible kind (EV-ADVIS-06006-02) is an ACCIDENT on Upper Serangoon Road near Kovan MRT, a road that appears nowhere on the recommended route (Rivervale Crescent, Sengkang East Road, KPE, PIE, Eunos Road 8), so it does not intersect the recommended route and does not justify this reroute. The driver's account that the KPE was jammed and an accident was shown is a bare assertion; POL-RD-23 says an assertion of traffic with no such data on the route does not justify the reroute. The POL-RD-24 matrix therefore lands on row (d): not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km — refund of the excess distance fare in full. On the recorded figures that is 1.60 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.15 SGD, without surge, exactly the excess_distance_fare_sgd the fare record derives. The rider asked for 3.00 SGD, but the policy's measure of this wrong is the excess distance fare only, so 1.15 SGD is returned and the balance of the claim is not granted. The driver's advocate argued the traffic question is unresolvable and the case should escalate; it is resolvable — the traffic data for the recommended route segment shows nothing — and the rider's alternative path (row (b), traffic-justified but uninformed) also yields the same 1.15 SGD, so the amount does not depend on that question. All artifacts relied on (trip record, chat log, fare breakdown and the two traffic advisories) are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0; the contested value of 3.00 SGD is below the 10.00 SGD threshold at which POL-GEN-22 makes an AI ruling final; neither profile carries a fraud flag; and POL-RD-25's 0.80 confidence floor is met, so no escalation is required. No referral arises on a route deviation in this policy version."
