    "explanation": "To both parties: the dispute is decided on the platform's recorded distances and the live traffic data, and part of the fare is returned to the rider.\n\nDeviation (POL-RD-22). The trip record (EV-TRIP-06006, weight 1.0) records 11.5 km actually driven against a recommended 9.9 km, a deviation of 1.60 km. That is over the 1.0 km tolerance, so the no-refund tolerance rows of the POL-RD-24 matrix (rows (c) and (e)) are unavailable. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-06006, weight 1.0) independently shows the same sequence of roads - the vehicle on Hougang Avenue 2 from 12:33:36 and Airport Road to 12:43:13 - used only to show which route was taken, as POL-RD-22 directs.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23). The reroute is not justified. The LTA record for the KPE segment the driver actually left (EV-ADVIS-06006-01, weight 1.0), which overlaps the trip window, is type NONE with speed bands 5-6 - no congestion, incident or closure on the recommended route. The one advisory of a qualifying kind (EV-ADVIS-06006-02, weight 1.0) is an ACCIDENT on Upper Serangoon Road near Kovan MRT, a road that appears on neither the recommended route (Rivervale Crescent, Sengkang East Road, KPE, PIE, Eunos Road 8) nor the route actually driven, so it does not intersect the recommended route and does not justify the reroute. The driver's account of a jam on the KPE is contradicted by the free-flowing speed bands on that segment. This answers the driver's argument that the traffic fact is left open: the record is complete, and I decide from the advisory's road, direction and location that it is not on the route.\n\nNotice (POL-RD-21). The rider was not informed. The chat log (EV-CHAT-06006, weight 1.0) carries 0 messages and the trip record shows no in-app calls and no recording, so a verbal notice cannot be established.\n\nRefund matrix (POL-RD-24). Row (d) applies - not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km - which refunds the excess distance fare in full: 1.60 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.15 SGD, with no surge. The same 1.15 SGD would be owed on row (b) had the reroute been justified, since the rider was not informed, so the result does not turn on the traffic question. The rider's full claim of 3.00 SGD is not payable: the policy's measure of this wrong is the excess distance fare only, which caps any recovery at 1.15 SGD. The rider's position is therefore a PARTIAL_REFUND of 1.15 SGD, part of the trip's charge returned. The present state is a fare of 15.40 SGD charged with refund_issued_sgd of 0.00, so 1.15 SGD is outstanding and is returned to the rider.\n\nNo escalation. The facts the matrix needs are established, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged. The contested value is 3.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD threshold, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence, and neither profile carries a fraud flag, so no higher requirement arises. All eight artifacts are COMPLETE at weight 1.0. POL-RD-25 requires a confidence of 0.80 and this ruling is at 0.90; the 2 km AI-deviation limb is not applied because route_deviation.thresholds.ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false, and the deviation is 1.60 km in any event. No clause in this category produces a referral, so none is made.",
